EXTENSION "ARMDef_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_WarringFamilies_FatherHerbertTheVillagePriest" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Tales of Mythic Europe - Father Herbert, the Village Priest"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-09"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_Core_Ext"

    # Father Herbert, the Village Priest (Chapter Nine: Warring Families, p139): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t1009631e06a1aab5d15f0c ^"Father Herbert, the Village Priest" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +1, Per +2, Pre 0, Com +1, Str –1, Sta 0, Dex 0, Qik 0"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "32 (32)"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "0 (4)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Priest; Privileged Upbringing, Student of the Divine; Depressed, Meddler, Vow"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Depressed +4, Self-conscious +3, Pious +2, Talkative +2"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "Village priest +3 (local), Blabbermouth +2 (local)"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Fist: Init 0, Attack +1, Defense +1, Damage –1"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+0"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "[Area] Lore 3 (geography), Artes Liberales 4 (logic), Awareness 3 (bored parishioners), Brawl 1 (dodging), Charm 3 (clergy), Church Lore 4 (history), Concentration 3 (reading), Dominion Lore 3+2 (miracles), Etiquette 3 (the Church), Folk Ken 4 (villagers), Latin 4 (sermons), Leadership 2 (inspiring guilt), Music 1 (psalms), Native Language 5 (gossip), Teaching 3 (teaching Theology), Theology 4 (sermons)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "An old, bound copy of the Book of Matthew, scruffy priest’s robe, ornate crucifix carved from ivory."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Herbert dresses in scruffy black robes and wears an ornate cross around his neck."
            ^"Source" STRING "Tales of Mythic Europe"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 139
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Herbert is only recently arrived at the village, replacing the previous priest who died five years ago. Herbert is relatively young, and is still finding his way around the village. Originally from a cathedral school in a distant town, Herbert resents his posting in the village, which he sees as a dead end. This view means that he takes his duties with only a grain of seriousness, and is starting to despair that he will never leave.\n\nNot long ago, he embarrassed himself by getting involved in an interfamily feud — he broke the confidence of village elder Baldwin to Peter, and then to make it up to Baldwin, revealed a secret of Peter’s to Baldwin. This resulted in both Peter’s and Baldwin’s extended families boycotting his sermons for almost a year. In order to better find a niche, he has befriended Peter, who has started to champion Father Herbert with the villagers. This has resulted in the villagers slowly coming to see him as a figure of some authority and respect.\n\nThe one thing that Herbert finds remarkable and worthwhile in the village is the church’s reliquary. He is immensely proud that his church has such a valuable item in it, and one of his very few joys is to polish and clean it every week.\n\nSeveral months ago, Herbert accidentally dropped the reliquary, which broke off a valuable jewel fixed prominently on top. He tried to reattach it, but has since hidden the gem and hides the damaged face of the reliquary. He is too afraid to seek anyone’s help to fix it, since he believes that the villagers would be furious with him. The gem itself is hidden under his mattress."
    }

}
